@ 8.1.1 - Early Middle Japanese to Modern Japanese
# citation: Zhen Lin
	# NB: The ordering of these changes may be slightly anachronic.
	p > ɸ
	ɸ > w / V_V
	(w)e > je
	∅ > w / _o
	w > ∅ / ! _{a,o}
	au iu uu eu ou > ɔ:[+ long] ju:[+ long] u:[+ long] jo:[+ long] o:[+ long]
	j > ∅ / _e
	w > ∅ / _o
	w > ∅ / k_a
	ɸ > h / ! _u
	ɔ:[+ long] > o:[+ long]
	# “Affrication of /ti di/ probably happened very early. Denasalization of the
	# 			prenasalized stops happened relatively later. Final /m/ merged with /n/ at some point,
	# 			and [d͡ʒ] (from */dj/) and [ʒ] (< */zj/) also merged.”